Description: disk image writer for USB, SD and NVMe media
 kalip writes Linux ISO images and Raspberry Pi OS images to removable media
 and internal drives. Images can be opened from a local file or fetched from a
 URL, which is queried first so the file name, size and content type are known
 before anything is downloaded.
 .
 When the image is a Raspberry Pi OS image -- detected from its partition table
 rather than its file name -- first boot settings can be seeded into custom.toml
 on the boot partition: hostname, user account, SSH keys and password login,
 wireless network and locale.
 .
 The graphical interface never runs as root. Only a small non-graphical helper
 is elevated through polkit, which is why it works on Wayland sessions where
 applications that elevate their whole user interface fail. The helper
 re-validates the target device on its own and refuses to write to any disk
 holding a mounted system filesystem or swap.
